{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head f78729635d7a16ead65de3e2e5b3842ec3ef5473, resting on all nine artifacts with docs/protocol.md first. Independently read the complete revision-2 delta and credited the seven byte-identical revision-1 artifacts already reviewed. Both findings in 1fe39980 are resolved at the contract level.\n\nArchitecture: R-CARRY-16 now gives each immutable snapshot an initially empty repository containing only its exact commit/tree/blob closure, under one fixed ref. Reuse is restricted to the same snapshot identity, with a separate read token per job; different snapshots never share object authority. The A/B/G responsibilities include creation, commit-ID verification, credentials and durable retirement. Sealed carry decisions, current runner attestation, the canonical-to-filtered snapshot binding, advisory checks and two-way volatile equality remain specified. The L decoder/replay gate must land before Room emits check-carried entries. This approves the amended contract and additive types, not completion of those runtime implementations.\n\nSecurity: exact current-snapshot object authority is now explicit even when an older SHA is known. Independently modeled the revised layout with real local Git: fetching and checking out the current snapshot succeeded; attempts to fetch the known older commit, tree and blob failed; only the current ref was advertised. This is a local object-set isolation test, not a live Artifacts/token test. The acceptance cases also retain concurrent different jobs, changed checker configuration, per-job tokens and cleanup outages. R-EXEC-8 now states the actual operator boundary: only trusted Room producers may bind to the harness; production exposes no public job route; service bindings alone do not verify an asserted job's origin. Token/repository cleanup is recorded before I/O and retried until confirmed.\n\nSimplification: one immutable object set and one ref per snapshot make the read boundary inspectable without relying on checkout behavior, parentlessness, undisclosed object IDs or removing refs. The revised lane edits and acceptance cases make this a concrete implementation contract. The explicitly open jj root-fact/history route remains future work within the complete scope, not a functionality waiver.\n\nValidation at this exact detached head: npm ci; root strict typecheck; complete npm test (118 Git Node, 100 Log Node, 95 Log Workers, 190 Policy Node, 189 Policy Workers passed with one existing skip, 88 UI); supplementary eight Git Workers tests; local real-Git snapshot isolation assertions. All passed; worktree clean. Full A/B/G/L implementation and live integration reviews remain required.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9901c32e31d601481da3a1c634da542acebbf2fa","binding":"assigned","head":"f78729635d7a16ead65de3e2e5b3842ec3ef5473","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e5093ea3726003a826b4dd3638e56f41b0eaecd5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c77b3003ce0ad6003894e3452cf3c2aa1a7584b2\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e5093ea3726003a826b4dd3638e56f41b0eaecd5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}